{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/91552-setting-hack-there-s-a-little-wolf-in-everyone","id":91552,"title":"Setting hack: There's A Little Wolf in Everyone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-15T05:08:56-07:00","id":91552,"title":"Setting hack: There's A Little Wolf in Everyone","content":"Setting hack: anyone at all can, potentially, become a werewolf. Father Wolf's blood is in no way a necessary requirement for experiencing a First Change, although it might increase the probability of becoming a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Many werewolves believe that an external, spiritual agent is the cause of the First Change. The commonly told Forsaken myth is that the crazy old mother moon gets to pick and choose who turns into a wolf according to her insane whim. Others prefer to believe that some remnant of Father Wolf's essence imbues people with wolfiness.<br /> <br /> There are some among the Pure who think they've been chosen by their tribal totems directly - some Predator Kings might think that Dire Wolf elevated them above humanity. And, in at least a few cases, spirit servants of the Maeljin have been seen in the vicinity of victims of the First Change closely after changing. Whether or not these werewolves have a higher change of becoming Bale Hound is not known.<br /> <br /> Some Iron Masters choose to believe that it's humans who, on some unconscious level, decide who should protect them from the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's no external influence involved. Maybe werewolf bites *do* cause the First Change, or at least increase the likelihood of turning into a wolf one day.<br /> <br /> The point is, the First Change could happen to anyone, at any time; and the exact circumstances are not known to the Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link